        {
          "path": "_m/g/f/5/c/duart-castle-wp/duart-castle-31108220397.jpg",
          "filename": "Duart Castle (31108220397).jpg",
          "caption": "The Castle was probably built by Clan MacDougall in the 13th century, and then fell into the hands of Clan MacLean in the 14th. with the Keep was perhaps built for Lachlan Lubanach. House added for Sir Allan Maclean. Passed to Earl of Argyll 1692 and abandoned 1751. Castle fell into decay, but was bought back in 1911 by Colonel Sir Fitzroy Maclean and was restored for him by Sir John James Burnet.",
          "alt": "The Castle was probably built by Clan MacDougall in the 13th century, and then fell into the hands of Clan MacLean in the 14th. with the Keep was perhaps built for Lachlan Lubanach. House added for Sir Allan Maclean. Passed to Earl of Argyll 1692 and abandoned 1751. Castle fell into decay, but was bought back in 1911 by Colonel Sir Fitzroy Maclean and was restored for him by Sir John James Burnet.",
